4 Usage
*******

4.1 Basic Usage
===============

  1. Connect your digital voice recorder to your computer.

  2. Open an Emacs buffer where you want the transcription inserted.

  3. Run ‘M-x whisper-dvr’ or press ‘C-c w d’.

  4. Select an audio file from the completion list.

  5. Wait for the transcription to complete.

4.2 Changing the DVR Directory
==============================

If your DVR is mounted at a different location:

     M-x whisper-dvr-set-directory RET /path/to/dvr RET

4.3 Switching Between the SD Card and the Built-in Memory
=========================================================

Sony recorders keep recordings in two places, the built-in memory and a
removable SD card, and the two use different folder layouts.  Two
commands switch between them without a directory prompt:

     M-x whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-sd-card
     M-x whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-internal-memory

   Each command copies the matching customization variable into
‘whisper-dvr-directory’.  A prefix argument saves the value with
‘customize-save-variable’ so that the choice outlives the session:

     C-u M-x whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-sd-card

   The directory is set even when the volume is not mounted, so either
command can be run before the recorder is plugged in.

4.4 Interactive Commands
========================

‘whisper-dvr’
     List audio files from the DVR directory and transcribe the selected
     file.  Default keybinding: ‘C-c w d’.  When
     ‘whisper-dvr-llm-postprocess’ is non-nil, the raw transcript is
     then structured by an LLM (*note LLM Post-Processing::).  A prefix
     argument inverts that setting for one run.

‘whisper-dvr-set-directory’
     Interactively set the DVR directory path.

‘whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-sd-card’
     Reset the DVR directory to ‘whisper-dvr-sd-card-directory’.  With a
     prefix argument, save the value for later sessions.

‘whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-internal-memory’
     Reset the DVR directory to ‘whisper-dvr-internal-memory-directory’.
     With a prefix argument, save the value for later sessions.

‘whisper-dvr-transcribe-file’
     Transcribe one audio file without the selection menu.  This is the
     entry point used by batch transcription and by the automatic device
     handlers.

‘whisper-dvr-toggle-auto-delete’
     Turn automatic deletion of processed recordings on or off for the
     current session (*note Automatic Deletion::).  With a prefix
     argument, pick the timing from a list.


