5 LLM Post-Processing
*********************

whisper.el returns a raw transcript.  When ‘whisper-dvr-llm-postprocess’
is non-nil, whisper-dvr sends that raw text in the background to a large
language model that applies the transcript-parser skill.  The skill
returns a LaTeX fragment with ‘\subsubsection’ headings, ‘\index’ keys,
one sentence per line, expanded contractions, corrected grammar, and a
closing list of TODO items.

   Think of whisper.el as a court reporter who takes down every word,
and of the LLM as the editor who turns that record into a clean
document.  The editor works in a separate process, so Emacs stays
responsive.

5.1 How it works
================

  1. ‘whisper-dvr’ transcribes the selected recording, and whisper.el
     inserts the raw text at point.
  2. whisper-dvr captures the text through
     ‘whisper-after-transcription-hook’ and ‘whisper-after-insert-hook’.
  3. The text goes to the backend named by ‘whisper-dvr-llm-backend’.
  4. The answer replaces the raw text, follows it, or opens in its own
     buffer, according to ‘whisper-dvr-llm-insert-method’.

   The raw transcript is never lost.  A failed or timed out request
leaves it in place.  When the raw text was edited while the model was
working, the result is inserted after it instead of replacing it.

   A prefix argument to ‘whisper-dvr’ inverts
‘whisper-dvr-llm-postprocess’ for one run.

5.2 Choosing the model or harness
=================================

‘claude-code’
     Claude Code in print mode.  The harness loads the skill named by
     ‘whisper-dvr-llm-skill-name’ from its own skills directory.

‘anthropic’
     The Anthropic Messages API through curl.  The body of
     ‘whisper-dvr-llm-skill-file’ becomes the system prompt.

‘openai-compatible’
     Any OpenAI style chat completions server.  Ollama, the llama.cpp
     server, LM Studio, and vLLM all qualify, so this backend runs the
     skill with a local model.

‘command’
     Any shell command that reads the prompt on standard input and
     prints the answer.  Every ‘%m’ in ‘whisper-dvr-llm-command’ is
     replaced by the model name.

‘function’
     An Emacs Lisp function called with the instructions, the
     transcript, a callback, and an error callback.  This backend suits
     gptel or ellama.

     ;; Claude Code as the harness.
     (setq whisper-dvr-llm-postprocess t
           whisper-dvr-llm-backend 'claude-code)

     ;; A local model served by Ollama.
     (setq whisper-dvr-llm-backend 'openai-compatible
           whisper-dvr-llm-model "qwen2.5:14b")

     ;; The Anthropic API.  The key comes from ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or
     ;; from auth-source for the host api.anthropic.com.
     (setq whisper-dvr-llm-backend 'anthropic
           whisper-dvr-llm-model "claude-sonnet-5-5")

5.3 LLM commands
================

‘whisper-dvr-toggle-llm-postprocess’
     Turn post-processing of new transcripts on or off.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-select-backend’
     Choose the backend and the model for the current session.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-process-region’
     Post-process the active region, or the whole buffer when no region
     is active.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-process-file’
     Read a transcript file such as ‘notes.txt’ and write
     ‘notes_parsed.tex’ beside it.  With a prefix argument, visit the
     new file.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-cancel’
     Cancel every running request.  The raw text stays in place.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-test-backend’
     Send a short sample transcript to the configured backend and report
     the result.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-show-log’
     Show the command, exit code, standard error, and standard output of
     each LLM run.  Claude Code writes many of its errors to standard
     output, so check here when a failure message is unclear.

5.4 LLM settings
================

‘whisper-dvr-llm-postprocess’
     Non-nil sends new transcripts to the LLM. Default ‘nil’.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-backend’
     The LLM or harness that runs the skill.  Default ‘claude-code’.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-model’
     Model name, or ‘nil’ for the default in
     ‘whisper-dvr-llm-default-models’.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-default-models’
     Fallback model for each backend.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-api-url’
     Endpoint for the HTTP backends, or ‘nil’ for the default.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-api-key’
     A string, a function that returns a string, or ‘nil’ to read the
     environment and then auth-source.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-skill-name’
     The skill the harness is asked to run.  Default
     ‘"transcript-parser"’.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-skill-file’
     The SKILL.md file whose body instructs the other backends.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-default-instructions’
     A condensed copy of the skill used when the skill file is missing.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-claude-program’
     Path to Claude Code.  Emacs started from the macOS Dock may need a
     full path.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-claude-prompt’
     The prompt passed to ‘claude -p’.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-claude-args’
     Extra arguments for Claude Code.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-claude-unset-env’
     Environment variables removed before Claude Code runs.  The default
     removes ‘ANTHROPIC_API_KEY’, so Claude Code uses the Pro or Max
     subscription login instead of billing an API key.  A "Credit
     balance is too low" error means the key was used.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-claude-embed-skill’
     Non-nil also passes the skill text with ‘--append-system-prompt’.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-command’
     Command line for the ‘command’ backend.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-function’
     Function for the ‘function’ backend.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-insert-method’
     One of ‘replace’, ‘append’, or ‘buffer’.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-output-buffer-name’
     Buffer used by the ‘buffer’ method.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-timeout’
     Seconds before a request is abandoned.  Default 900.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-max-tokens’
     Output token limit for the HTTP backends.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-temperature’
     Sampling temperature, or ‘nil’ for the server default.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-curl-program’
     Path to curl.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-wait-message’
     Notice shown in the echo area while the LLM works.  The default
     reads "Please wait, the LLM is parsing the transcript.  This step
     can take several minutes."  Set it to ‘nil’ to show nothing.

‘whisper-dvr-llm-after-process-hook’
     Functions called with the start and end of the inserted result.


