6 Automatic Deletion
********************

Without this feature a session ends with three steps.  You transcribe
the recording, delete it from the DVR, and eject the DVR. When
‘whisper-dvr-auto-delete-audio’ is non-nil, whisper-dvr removes the
audio file from the DVR as soon as its processing has succeeded, so the
next step is ‘M-x whisper-dvr-eject’.

   Think of the recording as a library book on loan.  It goes back to
the shelf only after you have finished every chapter you asked for.
When the LLM runs, the last chapter is the parsed transcript.  When it
does not, the last chapter is the raw transcript.

     (setq whisper-dvr-auto-delete-audio 'after-processing)
     ;; Free the space on the recorder at once.
     (setq whisper-dvr-auto-delete-method 'delete)

6.1 When the recording is removed
=================================

‘nil’
     The recording is kept.  This is the default.

‘after-processing’
     The recording is removed once the last requested stage succeeds.
     With LLM post-processing, that stage is the delivery of the parsed
     text, so a failed, timed out, or cancelled request keeps the file.
     Without the LLM, the file is removed once the raw transcript is
     inserted.

‘after-transcription’
     The recording is removed as soon as whisper.el inserts a non-empty
     raw transcript, even when the LLM fails later.

6.2 Safety rules
================

   • Only files inside a DVR location are removed.  These locations are
     ‘whisper-dvr-directory’, ‘whisper-dvr-sd-card-directory’,
     ‘whisper-dvr-internal-memory-directory’, and the entries in
     ‘whisper-dvr-volume-mount-points’.
   • An empty transcript keeps the file.
   • A whisper.el run for a different file keeps the file.
   • With ‘after-processing’, the file stays when LLM post-processing
     was requested but could not start.
   • Only the interactive commands ‘whisper-dvr’ and
     ‘whisper-dvr-transcribe-file’ delete files.  Batch and automatic
     transcription do not.

6.3 Deletion settings
=====================

‘whisper-dvr-auto-delete-audio’
     When to remove a processed recording.  One of ‘nil’,
     ‘after-processing’, or ‘after-transcription’.  Default ‘nil’.

‘whisper-dvr-auto-delete-method’
     How the recording is removed.  The value ‘default’ follows
     ‘whisper-dvr-use-trash’, ‘trash’ always uses the trash, and
     ‘delete’ removes the file permanently.  A file trashed from a
     removable volume may stay on that volume in a hidden trash folder,
     so ‘delete’ is the choice that frees the space at once.

‘whisper-dvr-auto-delete-hook’
     Functions called with the path of each removed recording.


