9 Troubleshooting
*****************

9.1 LLM post-processing skipped or failed
=========================================

A warning that LLM post-processing was skipped means Emacs could not
find ‘claude’, ‘curl’, or the configured command.  Set
‘whisper-dvr-llm-claude-program’ to a full path.  When a request fails,
the raw transcript stays in the buffer and the message names the cause,
such as an HTTP 401 for a bad key or a timeout for a long recording on a
slow local model.

9.2 DVR directory does not exist
================================

Ensure your DVR is connected and mounted.  Check the mount path with:

     ls /Volumes/  # macOS
     ls /media/    # Linux

9.3 No audio files found
========================

Verify that:
   • The directory path is correct
   • The directory contains files with supported extensions
   • File permissions allow reading

9.4 Transcription starts recording instead of transcribing
==========================================================

This was a bug in versions prior to 0.2.0.  The issue occurred because
‘whisper-file’ in whisper.el changed from accepting a file path argument
to being an interactive-only function.

   Update to version 0.2.0 or later, which correctly calls ‘whisper-run’
with the file path directly.


